WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.870
It's Monday, November 16, and this is the Transhuman Daily.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.030
Here's your day in transhumanism, in 3 minutes flat.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.870
The weekend's best is about second chances.

00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:21.460
Through a brain implant, a woman with ALS sang again.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:24.330
And gene editing is giving a Melbourne m

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:26.680
an the immune system he was born without.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:35.260
A locked-in man communicated by implant for over a year,

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:37.740
and brain-to-text even ran on an iPhone.

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:43.550
Imperial took a cue from Doctor Octopus: a brain cap for extra robot arms,

00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:45.490
while your hands keep working.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:49.860
OpenAI's new ChatGPT Wallet lets its AI agents shop for you,

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:52.540
checking with you before every purchase.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:57.720
And Penn built soft robot muscles that tap piano keys gently or firmly,

00:00:57.720 --> 00:00:59.320
and hold a steady gaze.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.880
On to longevity. In monkeys,

00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:06.580
a single gene-editing infusion kept blood fats lower for three years.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.700
And Johns Hopkins scans show Alzheimer's shrinks t

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:13.900
wo brain areas up to a decade before memory slips.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.520
Yale found diet with exercise, and drugs like metformin,

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:21.780
turned ageing clocks back. Most supplements didn't.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:27.060
And MIT found the brain's deep-sleep rinse runs weaker in older adults.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.100
On to wellbeing.

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:36.620
Australia's GPs now have backing to prescribe time in nature, 20 minutes a day.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:40.740
And a US survey found pitching basic income as fair

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:44.050
ness lifted support among people who value equality.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:49.630
Now, the catch. Blood NAD, which longevity supplements try to boost,

00:01:49.630 --> 00:01:52.360
didn't drop with age in healthy adults.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:53.450
And just in case,

00:01:53.450 --> 00:01:58.740
neuroscientists proposed eight tests for whether lab-grown mini brains could become conscious.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:05.350
SpaceX caught a Starship back from orbit for the first time,

00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:07.030
though its booster was lost.

00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:10.080
Back on the ground,

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:14.170
socks that stiffen the arch cut the energy cost of walking by 2%.

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:18.880
Oh, and Floaty, a kestrel-inspired robot,

00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:22.030
rides updrafts like a bird to save battery.

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:28.520
A voice back, a life back, a rocket home. The future's full of second chances.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.510
Zoom out, and the line only goes up.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.440
And the future keeps arriving ahead of schedule.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.970
One day, all of this. Tomorrow, probably more.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.170
You've been watching the Transhuman Daily.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.140
Live long. See you tomorrow.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.600
Want more? Meet us in North Sydney on November 27.
